        },
        {
            "summary": "Private individuals are empowered as decentralized energy producers.",
            "explanation": "A significant characteristic of this community structure is the focus on PRIVATPERSONEN (private individuals) as crucial actors in the decentralized production of renewable energy. Through policy incentives and regulatory supports, such as the streamlined approval process provided by the Wohnungseigentumsgesetz, individual homeowners are encouraged and enabled to install PV systems. This grassroots-level empowerment increases renewable generation capacity and actively involves the public in Austria’s energy transition efforts, further democratizing the country's approach to sustainability [Data: Entities (75); Relationships (116)]."
