        },
        {
            "summary": "Legal reforms align with Austria’s broader climate and energy targets.",
            "explanation": "The amendment to the Wohnungseigentumsgesetz is purposefully aligned with Austria’s commitment to national and European climate and energy goals. By minimizing bureaucratic barriers and enhancing the legal certainty around PV installations for residential property owners, Austria is ensuring that legislative instruments work in concert with strategic climate objectives, maximizing adoption and impact [Data: Entities (67); Relationships (103, 143, 144)]."
        },
        {
            "summary": "PV system expansion fosters local resilience and public participation.",
            "explanation": "Increased access to photovoltaic technology not only decentralizes energy production but also improves the resilience of individual communities and localities against energy crises. Broader participation by property owners helps to anchor sustainability at the community level, strengthens the stability of local energy supply, and engenders a culture of climate responsibility among the populace [Data: Entities (66, 75, 95, 96); Relationships (116, 143, 144)]."
