    "summary": "This community is centered on Austrian citizens (BÜRGER:INNEN) who are playing a pivotal role in driving the country’s energy transition towards decentralized, renewable energy generation. Central to this structure are innovative participatory models, especially in the photovoltaic (PV) sector, where citizens are both beneficiaries and engines of change. Key connecting entities such as citizen participation (Partizipation), the local electricity market (Strommarkt), and local load management (Lokales Lastmanagement) establish new frameworks and incentives to facilitate greater citizen involvement, efficiency, and sustainability in energy production, distribution, and consumption. The relationships among these entities demonstrate a systemic pivot from top-down energy strategies to more distributed, community-led approaches, enabled by evolving policies and technological solutions.",
