        {
            "summary": "EAG as the Legislative Foundation of Austria’s PV Strategy",
            "explanation": "The Erneuerbaren-Ausbau-Gesetz (EAG) is the key legal framework enabling Austria's renewable energy and PV expansion. It directly informs the implementation of Austria’s photovoltaic strategy by defining the regulatory and incentive landscape. The law is central for both market participants and policymakers, shaping the available instruments to promote large-scale PV deployment and integrating market mechanisms such as the market premium. This structure ensures clear alignment between national energy strategy and on-the-ground project development [Data: Entities (135); Relationships (204, 220)]."
