{
    "title": "Renewable Energy Building Regulations in Austria: Neubau and Sanierung Requirements",
    "summary": "This community centers on the regulatory landscape for buildings (Gebäude) in Austria concerning renewable energy integration, particularly the obligation to install photovoltaic (PV) systems during new construction (Neubau) and renovation (Sanierung) events. Recent policy changes have created direct links between building development or refurbishment and mandates for solar energy solutions, fundamentally shifting legal compliance expectations and technical requirements for the built environment. These relationships illustrate a systemic effort to increase the renewable energy footprint in Austria’s real estate sector.",
