            "summary": "Substantial implications for Austria’s renewable energy targets.",
            "explanation": "By legislating direct PV installation requirements for both new and renovated buildings, Austria is positioning its real estate sector as a major contributor to national renewable energy targets. The widespread application of these obligations has the potential to significantly increase distributed renewable energy generation capacity, reduce greenhouse gas emissions, and enhance building energy efficiency across the country [Data: Entities (91, 97, 98); Relationships (139, 140)]."
        },
        {
            "summary": "Reputational and business opportunities for compliant actors.",
            "explanation": "Organizations and firms able to effectively navigate and comply with these regulations stand to benefit reputationally and competitively. Compliance demonstrates a tangible commitment to sustainability and positions participants advantageously in procurement and project bidding landscapes influenced by increasingly stringent environmental criteria [Data: Entities (91, 97, 98)]."
        }
    ],
